::kind(api)

::meta{crate: sisho-counter, dependencies: list(sisho-run, sisho-tools), dependents: list(sisho-cli)}

=[sisho-counter]

The operating dashboard and counter for sisho.

Two-tier design:

- @strong[Board]: Status of tools, extensions, integrity check outcomes, and broken links.
- @strong[Counter]: Action prompt bar to run check, fix, check-links, or open desk.

==[Module editor]

===[Functions]

====[fn resolve_editor]

Resolve an editor command to open `file` at `line`.

Precedence chain:
1. `$SISHO_EDITOR` (handles `{file}`, `{line}`, `{col}` templates, extension words, or commands)
2. `$VISUAL` (Unix full-screen editor: nvim, vim, hx, etc.)
3. `$EDITOR` (Unix standard editor)
4. `sisho-desk` (if installed and active)
5. `nano` (system fallback)

====[fn resolve_editor_with_lookup]

==[Module links]

The link check as the counter shows it: what `tomet check-links --json`
reports about the links of a vault that point at nothing.

`tomet` does the check, with the cache it keeps outside the vault; this
runs it and reads the one JSON object it writes (the contract is
`tomet`'s, in `spec/cli/check-links.tmt` there).

===[Structs]

====[struct Position]

A line and a column, both counted from 1.

====[struct BrokenLink]

A link whose target does not exist.

====[struct Unreadable]

A document that could not be looked at.

====[struct Report]

What a run found.

===[Functions]

====[fn check]

Check the links under `dir` by running `tomet check-links --json`.

`Err` is why there is no report: `tomet` is not installed, or it could not
do the check (a path that is not there, a cache that cannot be opened). A
broken link is not an error; `tomet` exits 1 for it and the report is
there all the same.

==[Module model]

===[Structs]

====[struct ExtensionItem]

An extension presented on the Board.

====[struct ToolStatus]

Status of a core tool.

====[struct Model]

The state of the counter and board.

===[Enums]

====[enum StepSlot]

A slot representing a check step in progress or completed.

====[enum FocusedPane]

The currently focused pane on the Board.

====[enum WorkerMessage]

Messages sent from background threads to the model.

==[Module screen]

===[Structs]

====[struct Screen]

Terminal guard: manages raw mode, alternate screen, and mouse capture.
Ensures terminal is restored to normal state even on panic or error.

===[Functions]

====[fn restore_terminal]

Restore the terminal to cooked mode and exit alternate screen. Safe to call multiple times.

==[Module ui]

===[Functions]

====[fn draw]

Render the complete sisho-counter interface (Board + Counter).

==[Functions]

===[fn run]

Run the interactive counter TUI.
